This is a very common Java interview question.

equalsIgnoreCase() vs compareToIgnoreCase() :

Feature	       equalsIgnoreCase()	                              compareToIgnoreCase()
Purpose	       Checks if two strings are equal (ignoring case)	  Compares two strings lexicographically (ignoring case)
Return Type	   boolean	                                          int
Returns	       true or false	                                  Negative, 0, or Positive
Use When	   You only want to know if strings are equal	      You want to compare or sort strings